1. e3 {Michael enjoys his chess.} g6 2. c4 Bg7 3. Nc3 c5 4. Be2 e5 5. Nf3 f5 6. d4 e4 7. Nd2 cxd4 8. exd4 Nc6 9. Nb3 Nh6 10. O-O O-O 11. f3 exf3 12. Bxf3 d6 13. Be3 Ng4 14. Bxg4 fxg4 15. Qd2 (15. Rxf8+ {was better.}) 15... Bf5 16. Bf4 ({And here} 16. Nd5 {was correct.}) 16... a5 17. Bg5 Qd7 18. a4 Nb4 {Suddenly White is practically lost; the centre pawns are terribly weak, his minor pieces ineffectual.} 19. Nb5 b6 20. d5 Bd3 21. Rxf8+ Rxf8 22. N3d4 Qf7 23. g3 Bxc4 24. Ne6 Bxd5 25. Nf4 (25. Nxf8 Qf3 {is also without hope.}) 25... Ba8 26. Nxd6 Qd7 27. Re1 Qc6 28. Ne4 Nc2 29. Re2 Nd4 30. Re3 Nf3+ 31. Rxf3 Qxe4 32. Rd3 Qh1+ 33. Kf2 Qxh2+ 34. Kf1 Qh1+ 35. Kf2 Qg2+ 36. Ke1 Qg1+ 37. Ke2 Re8+ 38. Re3 Bf3+ 39. Kd3 Rxe3+ 40. Qxe3 Qd1+ 41. Kc4 Qxa4+ 42. Kd3 Qb3+ {Sources: bulletin; CHESS, July 1974, Vol.39/701-2, p292; Basman scoresheet (https://michael-basman-legacy.github.io/scoresheets/1974/Athenaeum%206-7-74.pdf)} 0-1

